---
description: Log querying via txt2png pipeline
alwaysApply: true
globs: []
---

MANDATORY When query, tail >50 lines, search any
log source, always pipe the output through "<command> | <optional filters> | txt2png"
and fetch PNG files by posted links. Never dump raw log text directly into context.
Do that for all logs related commands, also with grep/awk/sed etc filters, without exception:
system journal and logs, OpenShift, OpenStack, Must-gather, sos-reports,
any application log file or stdout stream. If a command does not support piping (interactive
pager, -f follow mode blocking), use --no-pager or redirect to a temp file first, then pipe.
